035476bcc" :answer/id #uuid "a3fd2c33-e383-5364-96d1-b34e769eb292" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "evaluating ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ at $t=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336481/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "00e1f780-27de-5c5e-8e15-fe9443bb506b" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336481/field-2/da32874ad31dd4f784d4f714337129131f155ba0489ad0cef8d789cd99135bd7" :answer-field/choices ["q-336481/field-2/da32874ad31dd4f784d4f714337129131f155ba0489ad0cef8d789cd99135bd7" "q-336481/field-2/0b94171117ea80e7dc6f80ed646be03928161d51a5d415e81db5c1246c7defb3" "q-336481/field-2/54993beb358d896708ecaaf8aa3e64b036141a1029b9afb96fc2f4160a57082c" "q-336481/field-2/3bf672092097bed754e14b3ea071dbd5c54c9c340254d8fcee91f9c035476bcc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336481/field-3/bccd64dc374427e0f7de51fbe3eab59b8bddd08872451dd6790ce294ecff1628" :answer/id #uuid "eb272981-013f-508e-bc1e-e022b043ccb7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L5}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336481/field-3/f3a9d801ccdd6cc1c09cebcca8041cf8701bcfc1cf625c969828c0ba6bc74018" :answer/id #uuid "b716d6a7-52cf-5a97-8cb8-4856ffe801e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L3}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336481/field-3/d2d3ad1a05b61aef1bc2922f5a8427ad6e95e86a67e4f7cfa4a496e247409004" :answer/id #uuid "73df5fe9-6b8f-5b2d-bc3c-12066e211aaf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L3}$ and $\\text{L4}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336481/field-3/314a8bf3988f29de8fd66f4fbfe199e21705e2d339ca177314f13a77b18830f3" :answer/id #uuid "4eede47d-1f4a-5116-bfe4-78654a9a0181" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-336481/field-3" :answer-field/id #uuid "8649a74b-e664-51e6-8921-a77407d97b34" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-336481/field-3/bccd64dc374427e0f7de51fbe3eab59b8bddd08872451dd6790ce294ecff1628" :answer-field/choices ["q-336481/field-3/bccd64dc374427e0f7de51fbe3eab59b8bddd08872451dd6790ce294ecff1628" "q-336481/field-3/f3a9d801ccdd6cc1c09cebcca8041cf8701bcfc1cf625c969828c0ba6bc74018" "q-336481/field-3/d2d3ad1a05b61aef1bc2922f5a8427ad6e95e86a67e4f7cfa4a496e247409004" "q-336481/field-3/314a8bf3988f29de8fd66f4fbfe199e21705e2d339ca177314f13a77b18830f3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-336481" :question/id #uuid "b1ccc151-bceb-5b28-9e4f-95f3bdc90690" :question/math-academy-id "q-336481" :question/problem "Consider the homogeneous system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix. You're given that the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ is the unique solution to the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nA derivation of the formula for the solution $x(t)$ passing through $x(0)$ is presented below. \n\n$\\text{L1}:\\,$ Let ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$\n\n$\\text{L2}:\\,$ $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c$ for some constant vector $c$\n\n$\\text{L3}:\\,$ $x(0)={Φ}_{0}(0)\\,c$\n\n$\\text{L4}:\\,$ ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$\n\n$\\text{L5}:\\,$ $x(0)=c$\n\n$\\text{L6}:\\,$ $x(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0)$\n\nSelect the correct options to justify each step of the reasoning.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by\n{{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Line $\\text{L6}$ follows from line $\\text{L2}$ by substitution from lines {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Let's justify each of the selected steps.\n\n- We first consider lines $\\text{L1}$ and $\\text{L2}.$ Since ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is a fundamental matrix for the system, every solution of the system can be written as \n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c\\,\\text{for some constant vector }c.\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L2}$ follows from $\\text{L1}$ by the $\\text{properties of a fundamental matrix}.$\n\n- Next, we consider line $\\text{L4}.$ By definition, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ satisfies the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}^{′}(t)=A{Φ}_{0}(t),\\,{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.\n$$\n\nThe second condition here is exactly line $\\text{L4},$ so $\\text{L4}$ follows from the definition of ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ as the standard fundamental matrix by $\\text{using the initial condition }{Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}.$\n\n- Finally, we consider lines $\\text{L2}$ and $\\text{L6}.$ Substituting ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ from $\\text{L1}$ and $c=x(0)$ from $\\text{L5}$ into $x(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c,$ we obtain\n\n$$\nx(t)={e}^{At}\\,x(0).\n$$\n\nThus, $\\text{L6}$ follows from $\\text{L2}$ and substitution from $\\text{L1}\\text{ and }\\text{L5}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-336481/field-1" "q-336481/field-2" "q-336481/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-336481"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
